From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:17:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/57] docs/plan.md: where the Z 6III stands -- phases 0-6
 worked through, what does not work, what is next

The plan still described the display, input, CFexpress and capture as
future phases and the RTOS as stopping at the graphics engine. It now
opens with what is measured as of 3ac1f42 (boot with Linux to BusyBox,
menus, keys, live view, a still written to the card, standby, JPEG
decode), ranks what is known not to work (playback's resize, the other
shutter types, the late d6 change, wake from standby, settings not
persisting), and proposes the order for next: re-enable smoke's Linux
check (z63-tools/frontier still records 0x15540000, which no longer
stops anything), playback's resize, wake from standby, the shutter
types, persistence. The method and the history are kept short; the
rules are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
